# L §2.1 ("A four-digit literal is a year where a period is expected"), §2.5 (a key-list variable takes its index from
# its key positions; here it has none) and §4.1: y over [2026, 2027] as a span end is the year.  pay books 10.00 PLN on
# day 5 of every month into world: flows(world, y) is 12 x 10.00 = 120.00 PLN each year (L §5.14.3), as the literal
# form q2 gives.  The binding prints its key as written.
# (Writer 8: L §5.10 refuses a unit stated on a place whose kind isn't of unit one, so `outside PLN` is gone; the place
# read by flows is now a thing of its own outside kind of one unit, `kind payees: place PLN signed outside`, since
# flows of a place of unit any is refused, L §5.14.3.)
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source s "x"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
kind payees: place PLN signed outside
place world: payees lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input dom: int

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN
  dom = 5
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

ask q: flows(world, y) for y in [2026, 2027]
ask q2: flows(world, 2026), flows(world, 2027)
=== expect
q (y = 2026): 120.00 PLN
...
q (y = 2027): 120.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-18
q2: (120.00 PLN, 120.00 PLN)
...
